  grid: 10x10, bg=black(0)
  markers:
    count: 4-6 isolated pixels of a single fg color (azure/8) [observed]
    max_per_row: exactly 2 (rows with markers have 1 or 2)
    max_per_col: exactly 2 (cols with markers have 1 or 2)
    placement: rows 1-9, cols 1-9; no marker on row 0 or col 0 [observed]
  lines:
    horizontal: 1-2 lines (rows containing exactly 2 markers); span length 4-7
    vertical: 1-2 lines (cols containing exactly 2 markers); span length 4-7
    total: 2-4 lines per grid
    isolated_markers: exactly 1 marker belongs to neither a horizontal nor vertical line [observed]
  transform:
    for each row/col with 2 markers, fill the entire span between them (inclusive) with fg color
    isolated markers and single-marker rows/cols remain unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Start with 10x10 black grid. Pick fg color (8).
    2. Decide line count: 1-2 horizontal + 1-2 vertical (total 2-4).
    3. For each horizontal line, pick a row and two distinct columns (span 4-7 cells).
       For each vertical line, pick a column and two distinct rows (span 4-7 cells).
       Ensure no row has >2 endpoints and no col has >2 endpoints.
    4. Draw all line spans on the output grid.
    5. Place exactly 1 isolated marker at a position whose row has no other marker
       and whose column has no other marker.
    6. To derive the input, keep only the endpoint markers (and the isolated marker);
       erase all filled span interiors.
    7. Validate: each row/col has at most 2 markers; exactly 1 isolated marker exists.
```
